<p>
  A <a href="https://github.com/basecamp/lexxy">Lexxy</a> editor running on <a
  href="https://github.com/jpcamara/lexxy-realtime">lexxy-realtime</a>. The
  room is a <code>Note</code> record. The client joins with a signed
  GlobalID scoped to that record and field, and the shared state is the
  <code>Y.XmlFragment</code> that Lexical keeps its document in.
</p>
<p>
  After every update, the server renders the whole document to HTML with
  <code>Y::Lexxy</code> and saves it into the note's plain <code>body</code>
  column. The output matches the editor's own serializer byte for byte. The
  panel below reads that column back over HTTP. Ruby produced it, without a
  browser.
</p>
